From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: disable autotuner sampling on A7xx to eliminate frame pacing jitter

On Adreno 7xx, dynamic autotuning queries hardware performance counters to
experiment with GMEM vs Sysmem passes. On the Snapdragon 8s Gen 3, counter
sampling introduces frame pacing jitter and micro-stutter during the first
minutes of gameplay.

This patch disables autotuner sampling on A7xx and defers directly to
our static cost model without runtime counter query overhead.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc
index b918231..8271a90 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_autotune.cc
@@ -100,6 +100,14 @@ tu_autotune_use_bypass(struct tu_autotune *at,
                        struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer,
                        const struct tu_render_pass *pass)
 {
+   /* Snapdragon 8s Gen 3 (SM8635 / Adreno 735):
+    * Disable runtime autotuner experimentation to eliminate
+    * frame pacing spikes from performance counter sampling.
+    * Fall back directly to our tuned GMEM cost calculation.
+    */
+   if (cmd_buffer->device->physical_device->info->chip >= 7)
+      return fallback_use_bypass(pass, cmd_buffer->state.framebuffer, cmd_buffer);
+
    if (!at->enabled || simultaneous_use)
       return fallback_use_bypass(pass, cmd_buffer->state.framebuffer, cmd_buffer);
 
